	"hardwareControls": [
		"88-key keyboard",
		"MASTER / PIANO: Master level, Piano A, Piano B, Piano select, Piano timbre, KB touch",
		"PROGRAM / SYNTH: Program display, Program dial, Synth A, Synth B, Attack, Release",
		"EFFECTS: Mod 1 rate, Mod 1 amount, Mod 2 rate, Mod 2 amount, Delay mix, Delay feedback, Reverb mix, Compressor amount"
	],
	"notice": "Kawai triple-sensor keyboard; no pitch stick or modulation wheel. Configure MIDI channel, Local Control and pedal type in the menus. The five-pin Triple Pedal 2 connector is a dedicated pedal connection, not a MIDI input. Match the instrument MIDI channel and receive filters before sending notes or CCs. USB carries MIDI/data rather than audio; connect the audio outputs separately. Consult the download page for the correct Windows USB driver. Port aliases have not been verified on hardware; select the profile manually. The drawings are selected-control schematics rather than scale panel plans. Keyboard and panel controls remain unbound; splits, octave shifts and layer routing can change their behavior. Only the listed CCs are supplied, not the full MIDI implementation.",
